perations \n\nI. ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}$\nII. ${R}_{3}:=…$\nIII. ${R}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below ${a}_{23}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 0 & -10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404530 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367d5c7f-38e0-520e-83c3-49e14d8a0120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-2{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404532} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd078f9-4afb-5657-b580-57e60ff58958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404533} {:answer/id #uuid "a9eefb87-41c8-5096-b981-c10f00b1b3e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404534} {:answer/