gned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -12 & -24 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -16 & -11 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-3{C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -12 & -24 & -13 & 5 \\\\ -16 & -11 & -17 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-5{C}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-3{C}_{4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30ba6213-39ae-5a81-9962-30d6ff7c4850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-7{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355087} {:answer/id #uuid "54734807-ae5c-597d-af1e-984fd026c789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355414} {:answer/id #uuid "772d99d4-23a3-5913-be91-c66582d35ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-7{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355712} {:answer/id #uuid "aac8ecc8-fdb4-5513-af23-621bc2e9a0e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+7{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356178} {:answer/id #uuid "f6a4c391-a5e2-5350-851f-fc2e85285e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+7{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356813}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355087} :answer-field/id #uuid "b439dc7a-fba4-5c3c-8d49-584df3ca4181" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0568247a-0893-5a83-bb65-a32f42d7293a" :question/math-academy-id "q-91214" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\n- ${C}_{1}:=…$\n- ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}$\n- ${C}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{43}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-7{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-7{C}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48b1c21b-17a8-5932-8da9-5e616c8cd523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-4{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400494} {:answer/id #uuid "466954de-a984-57a2-be5a-cd8d17a4da88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.ty