gin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1a477f1-10fc-50a1-981c-aae4b3c5dea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} - 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160713} {:answer/id #uuid "c0333c66-4f35-5f3c-9968-610aa5423fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 3R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} - 2R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160714} {:answer/id #uuid "f2355978-048f-57b5-8eee-c677498630a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} + 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160715} {:answer/id #uuid "175e8e59-45a0-515a-829f-30c1a15ea357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} + 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160716} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea804c1-eba2-5894-a0db-ce41e6af71d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} - 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160717}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3e10ff-3c11-531e-9e12-9a991205d1f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f91cfd00-78b8-5e81-b3da-fb66e4a255b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404525} {:answer/id #uuid "ba816428-2269-5d70-a23d-de4d9459d350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404526} {:answer/id #uuid "6b221426-9041-561c-a939-a652454c20be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404527} {:answer/id #uuid "7377369a-9c28-53fe-95a8-20a033d61460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404528} {:answer/id #uuid "4d223b12-1545-5649-89b4-f8afd0248272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404526} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ebe645c-97a3-5257-bc32-0836ea3ff9c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "200a95d9-6cef-55b2-a6a6-5c194d5765aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-91163" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{23}=-3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43a80e41-ea6d-5dc5-8544-cc70dca8d3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263596} {:answer/id #uuid "4b90aadb-f9e4-508b-92bf-073c268201e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263651} {:answer/id #uuid "940e5cc9-27d8-51d7-8f1d-549a3633ab6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264269} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a74a83-d4dc-5b30-95c5-487b782224a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264609} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5ad9b3-96d7-5c25-a4f3-7203412fccd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264807}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263651} :answer-field/id #uuid "5903ddc6-2868-58c2-b450-5bd4c4444b22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "53a04721-1169-5bfc-a82b-bd17c3d28e6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130444" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{32}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & -8 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "660f4f28-6bd6-5e7c-bf01-84615c79b680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263882} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff3d3ef-4f6c-5330-a962-bfb0eb8eaee3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263967} {:answer/id #uuid "8f348c95-8602-5808-80d0-ad38f452e80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264226} {:answer/id #uuid "97488787-23b6-520e-b6f2-b0cba1aee93a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264298} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2019a2-0875-5a3e-98b9-1ba45e406892" :answ