55-02a1ecec361e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "26e3c3e9-0f2f-55d8-b677-4d51648ddadf" :question/math-academy-id "q-91159" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{21}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "04f4431c-776f-545b-904c-b0fd1f0a5fab" :step/math-academy-id 30059 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162826}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162829 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161968 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161760 :question/id #uuid "f9912357-1d1d-5413-917e-257dc5dfc0fe" :question/math-academy-id "e-8051" :question/problem "![](images/94/941de9bd4837b4b5c9f0d2bf64c4ea0fd9be657b0368d03cac169742083822d1.png)\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_3,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of $a_{13}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+6{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+5{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & -17 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $C_1:=C_1+6C_3\\quad$ and $\\quad C_2:=C_2+5C_3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a941c4e1-5e36-53ce-bc6b-7d6663d0963c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} + 4C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} - 3C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160629} {:answer/id #uuid "f458abd4-da18-5702-90a4-330e62adc6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} + C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160630} {:answer/id #uuid "1dabc275-1f78-58e5-af0a-2f8732ba71e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} + 4C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160631} {:answer/id #uuid "34741622-1ae3-5eb4-ab55-84a7650c2729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} - 4C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160632} {:answer/id #uuid "5536cf5f-999a-5c38-9842-8c8dc2cc8268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/va