$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14dacd30-9d3f-53cb-b0f9-9d2f9507316d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263193} {:answer/id #uuid "156b2cc8-ac27-5d0b-85cb-de0cf638abe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263200} {:answer/id #uuid "322f025a-079b-5cfc-90c1-6a75a02f73bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-5{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+3{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263430} {:answer/id #uuid "5da97601-cba3-510d-90a7-f99d3bd64765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263813} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2b375e-cb9d-5388-b4c5-104e0f651bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263193} :answer-field/id #uuid "922b672c-88e3-5cd0-aa28-4833f6413211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f5b6d005-cac9-5d71-a15c-66f827fd6327" :question/math-academy-id "q-130610" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265940 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1498ab47-556d-5f86-9b51-5a2556aa636b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+4{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263192} {:answer/id #uuid "19def71b-5765-528d-b0f4-5a2e8748ba42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263247} {:answer/id #uuid "4056a8e7-718e-5f77-b56d-c9e482d80f9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263570} {:answer/id #uuid "858577f3-b658-525b-b5c6-fab27a1164cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264149} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9a562d-f5d3-5fe5-a15a-9fab41b8183d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263247} :an