atrix}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1a477f1-10fc-50a1-981c-aae4b3c5dea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} - 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160713} {:answer/id #uuid "c0333c66-4f35-5f3c-9968-610aa5423fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 3R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} - 2R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160714} {:answer/id #uuid "f2355978-048f-57b5-8eee-c677498630a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} + 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160715} {:answer/id #uuid "175e8e59-45a0-515a-829f-30c1a15ea357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} + 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160716} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea804c1-eba2-5894-a0db-ce41e6af71d1" :answer/ty