n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112d32b0-319b-55b9-b92b-0d23bba88ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354822} {:answer/id #uuid "76d39a59-aca5-5b5e-9d95-7c047e10b899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355707} {:answer/id #uuid "9563c6da-0097-5e94-9ae2-9bc7d6f4db8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355978} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cbddf4-d6db-5328-89d4-754473565ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356426} {:answer/id #uuid "cac9cab1-c0f0-59e8-86c6-60478192c099" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355978} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae3b5612-c9d4-5b4a-8d07-09bc7d4a467d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "be625aba-1e4a-556c-a78e-3cfc2c1b0666" :question/math-academy-id "q-91158" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 21\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{22}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "196fbdce-7928-5d41-b041-fcf74f8b8aa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354890} {:answer/id #uuid "2fe0be77-9f92-5dc0-8325-c4e3b1b80415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355080} {:answer/id #uuid "72ac8629-836e-5109-b4c1-d861ef64a9a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355673} {:answer/id #uuid "df704d25-850e-5878-8185-b5b2fa360681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356620} {:answer/id #uuid "fa1ed449-c755-5265-b246-b187a5b610aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-9{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356851}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355673} :answer-field/id #uuid "86286958-f4a9-548f-8084-a212af69f077" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5b61d5ca-7f09-5da1-b160-0e00fef59814" :question/math-academy-id "q-91160" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ -13 & 28 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below ${a}_{13}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ -13 & 28 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357502 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ca72af9-8564-5e6d-9a64-8fc990f69b9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355047} {:answer/id #uuid "2e69e2b0-e41b-5978-9da4-3a119daad7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355063} {:answer/id #uuid "9335f94b-1d46-578a-a317-1e95475f07f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355964} {:answer/id #uuid "b177b965-1d15-547c-b1bc-afd6537bfb98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356227} {:answer/id #uuid "b48573bd-ceec-5878-bb16-6b4d26b72e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356250}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355964} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a48285a-e13c-534f-8203-7071ee7ea25a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ee46ab50-1172-582c-9154-5604520f146c" :question/math-academy-id "q-91162" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{31}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a7281f6-7e60-5d96-9073-2b79663c148b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400473} {:answer/id #uuid "3d1c46db-e09e-574c-8457-d835d0d60cb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400474} {:answer/id #uuid "909cb4b3-d84a-5df3-b043-02b797c8f6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400475} {:answer/id #uuid "496f929c-182e-536d-8240-53d72e20d1ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400476} {:answer/id #uuid "1e501008-96e1-5873-9523-2270ec047af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400477}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400477} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ddf9b10-51fd-5a37-b528-b67408ad0ada" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fc4fe478-ecca-5d83-9a4b-47e34a0bc1c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130448" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below ${a}_{12}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b9183d1-23e9-5f90-a209-d6b19d245c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404512} {:answer/id #uuid "226f3fd1-f941-5569-80fa-d157db347e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404513} {:answer/id #uuid "3b46698e-ccc1-5f9f-8f8c-b005abd4b4b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404514} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4bce52-0e47-55a1-ac84-7a9f035eef89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404515} {:answer/id #uuid "38987e9b-2b2d-5194-a0c2-03820aac76b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404516}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404513} :answer-field/id #uuid "7222ce8b-9f86-5907-ac8e-304c68fbadee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bc8df3f8-8c99-53c4-bedf-bdbc4a64bd8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-91157" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -10 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -13 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{33}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -10 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -13 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404517 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73f5eb09-e668-558b-b5c4-5f72bb86b5f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404519} {:answer/id #uuid "b30692bb-6bff-5975-b521-cac176cbe736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404520} {:answer/id #uuid "0481513e-3cd0-504e-8e8e-90f5fc5b8b57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+7{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404521} {:answer/id #uuid "7e64580b-23e3-5c32-bb1a-f2f9628a7159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+7{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404522} {:answer/id #uuid "85047f08-97d3-5876-b80f-412bddff211b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-8{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-7{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404523}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404519} :answer-field/id #uuid "6844cde6-2278-591a-a355-02a1ecec361e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "26e3c3e9-0f2f-55d8-b677-4d51648ddadf" :question/math-academy-id "q-91159" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{21}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161968 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161760 :question/id #uuid "f9912357-1d1d-5413-917e-257dc5dfc0fe" :question/math-academy-id "e-8051" :question/problem "![](images/94/941de9bd4837b4b5c9f0d2bf64c4ea0fd9be657b0368d03cac169742083822d1.png)\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_3,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of $a_{13}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+6{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+5{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & -17 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $C_1:=C_1+6C_3\\quad$ and $\\quad C_2:=C_2+5C_3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a941c4e1-5e36-53ce-bc6b-7d6663d0963c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} + 4C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} - 3C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160629} {:answer/id #uuid "f458abd4-da18-5702-90a4-330e62adc6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} + C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160630} {:answer/id #uuid "1dabc275-1f78-58e5-af0a-2f8732ba71e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} + 4C_{3}$