/id #uuid "a68c2e7c-c605-5187-a1fa-13349acf01b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42917" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of ${a}_{33}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162572 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "124b8108-d70d-5e3c-828c-50d63b0cf6af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354832} {:answer/id #uuid "24a8a660-76f2-5a0f-9789-7ab3658591e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354970} {:answer/id #uuid "35ce6d1c-693e-5e83-8b9a-c30039c3ddcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355151} {:answer/id #uuid "5a28b797-a23b-5463-a9f7-6dfb98535d3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355460} {:answer/id #uuid "8579263d-73b1-5e7c-bcee-abc84781117a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355841}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355151} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f4aca94-1cff-5a77-9b5d-2bd96a266959" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "63dc72f5-1b5e-509c-b30f-0a4ab5f385d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-91189" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}=5$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26a6a529-cbbd-5a0e-aaf2-1d24fe040a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263338} {:answer/id #uuid "ac06dd13-879b-59f5-8b67-9f915ecfa721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+4{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264476} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4a7f32-e0d8-5b97-bf06-e077a7dc03db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264498} {:answer/id #uuid "b09ef022-7731-5eff-a524-13d430436d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264521} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d6343c-c5e3-58e2-b904-4bdcb1593623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263338} :answer-field/id #uuid "19441897-9d3b-593f-a806-716b82f4319e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "20588ade-71ed-551a-be45-9c686e3a54a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130609" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -2 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -2 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14dacd30-9d3f-53cb-b0f9-9d2f9507316d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263193} {:answer/id #uuid "156b2cc8-ac27-5d0b-85cb-de0cf638abe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263200} {:answer/id #uuid "322f025a-079b-5cfc-90c1-6a75a02f73bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-5{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+3{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263430} {:answer/id #uuid "5da97601-cba3-510d-90a7-f99d3bd64765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263813} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2b375e-cb9d-5388-b4c5-104e0f651bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263193} :answer-field/id #uuid "922b672c-88e3-5cd0-aa28-4833f6413211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f5b6d005-cac9-5d71-a15c-66f827fd6327" :question/math-academy-id "q-130610" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265940 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1498ab47-556d-5f86-9b51-5a2556aa636b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+4{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263192} {:answer/id #uuid "19def71b-5765-528d-b0f4-5a2e8748ba42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263247} {:answer/id #uuid "4056a8e7-718e-5f77-b56d-c9e482d80f9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263570} {:answer/id #uuid "858577f3-b658-525b-b5c6-fab27a1164cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264149} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9a562d-f5d3-5fe5-a15a-9fab41b8183d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263247} :answer-field/id #uuid "459b1236-8fdb-5818-8181-d8d6166d7571" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "999081e6-b687-59be-9094-b550515c9e09" :question/math-academy-id "q-130611" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30dc5728-5252-56fc-a0f8-75e1a4a34f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}: